  {"comment": "Three swatches kept with the strip's +, then a right press on the middle chip opens Rename and Remove. Rename takes 'Skin shadow' and Enter, and the chip's tooltip reads it before its hex. A second rename is thrown away by Escape. Remove puts 'Swatch removed' up with the undo chord, and Ctrl+Z under it puts the swatch back in its place with its name. A removal left until the notice has gone is given back by the menu's Undo remove instead. Last, the strip is saved as a GIMP palette, cleared, the GIMP fixture loaded with its names, and the saved file loaded after it. The s44 restart scenario opens on this run's profile and reads the names again."},
